@baseUrl = http://localhost:8080
@testDate = 2026-11-22

### Replace these values with IDs returned by your POST requests.
@memberId = 1
@roomId = 1
@deskId = 2
@bookingId = 1

### ==========================================================
### 1. MEMBERS
### ==========================================================

### 1.1 Get all members
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/members
Accept: application/json

###

### 1.2 Create a member
### Use a new email for each fresh test run.
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/members
Content-Type: application/json
Accept: application/json

{
  "fullName": "CoWorkHub Test User",
  "email": "coworkhub.test.20261121@example.com"
}

###

### 1.3 Get member by ID
### Replace @memberId with the ID returned by 1.2.
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/members/{{memberId}}
Accept: application/json

###

### 1.4 Get bookings for a member
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/members/{{memberId}}/bookings
Accept: application/json


### ==========================================================
### 2. RESOURCES - LISTING AND FILTERING
### ==========================================================

### 2.1 Get all resources
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/resources
Accept: application/json

###

### 2.2 Get resource by ID
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/resources/{{roomId}}
Accept: application/json

###

### 2.3 Filter resources by type - ROOM
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/resources?type=ROOM
Accept: application/json

###

### 2.4 Filter resources by type - DESK
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/resources?type=DESK
Accept: application/json

###

### 2.5 Filter resources by minimum capacity
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/resources?minCapacity=4
Accept: application/json

###

### 2.6 Filter resources by location
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/resources?location=Doha
Accept: application/json

###

### 2.7 Filter resources by maximum hourly price
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/resources?maxPrice=100
Accept: application/json

###

### 2.8 Combine resource filters
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/resources?type=ROOM&minCapacity=4&location=Doha&maxPrice=100
Accept: application/json


### ==========================================================
### 3. CREATE RESOURCES
### ==========================================================

### 3.1 Create a meeting room
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/resources/rooms
Content-Type: application/json
Accept: application/json

{
  "name": "HTTP Test Meeting Room",
  "location": "Doha",
  "capacity": 8,
  "hourlyRate": 75.0,
  "status": "ACTIVE",
  "hasProjector": true,
  "hasVideoConference": true
}

###

### 3.2 Create a desk
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/resources/desks
Content-Type: application/json
Accept: application/json

{
  "name": "Desk A1",
  "location": "Doha",
  "hourlyRate": 15.0,
  "status": "ACTIVE",
  "deskType": "STANDARD",
  "capacity": 1
}


### ==========================================================
### 4. RESOURCE AVAILABILITY
### ==========================================================

### 4.1 Find all available resources for a time interval
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/resources/available?startDateTime={{testDate}}T09:00:00&endDateTime={{testDate}}T10:00:00
Accept: application/json

###

### 4.2 Find available rooms
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/resources/available?startDateTime={{testDate}}T09:00:00&endDateTime={{testDate}}T10:00:00&type=ROOM
Accept: application/json

###

### 4.3 Find available desks
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/resources/available?startDateTime={{testDate}}T09:00:00&endDateTime={{testDate}}T10:00:00&type=DESK
Accept: application/json

###

### 4.4 Find resources for five attendees
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/resources/available?startDateTime={{testDate}}T09:00:00&endDateTime={{testDate}}T10:00:00&attendees=5
Accept: application/json

###

### 4.5 Find available rooms for five attendees
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/resources/available?startDateTime={{testDate}}T09:00:00&endDateTime={{testDate}}T10:00:00&attendees=5&type=ROOM
Accept: application/json


### ==========================================================
### 5. BOOKINGS - READ AND CREATE
### ==========================================================

### 5.1 Get all bookings
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/bookings
Accept: application/json

###

### 5.2 Get booking by ID
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/bookings/{{bookingId}}
Accept: application/json

###

### 5.3 Create a valid booking - SCREENSHOT TEST 1
### Create a booking
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/bookings?memberId={{memberId}}&resourceId={{deskId}}
Content-Type: application/json
Accept: application/json

{
  "startDateTime": "{{testDate}}T09:00:00",
  "endDateTime": "{{testDate}}T10:00:00",
  "attendees": 1,
  "totalCost": 15.0,
  "status": "CONFIRMED"
}

###

### 5.4 Create an overlapping booking - SCREENSHOT TEST 2
### Run after 5.3, with the SAME member/resource/time.
### Expected: 409 Conflict.
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/bookings?memberId=1&resourceId=2
Content-Type: application/json
Accept: application/json

{
  "startDateTime": "{{testDate}}T09:00:00",
  "endDateTime": "{{testDate}}T10:00:00",
  "attendees": 1,
  "totalCost": 15.0,
  "status": "CONFIRMED"
}

###

### 5.5 Create booking with invalid time interval - SCREENSHOT TEST 3
### Start time is after end time. Expected: 400 Bad Request.
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/bookings?memberId={{memberId}}&resourceId={{roomId}}
Content-Type: application/json
Accept: application/json

{
  "startDateTime": "{{testDate}}T15:00:00",
  "endDateTime": "{{testDate}}T14:00:00",
  "attendees": 2,
  "totalCost": 75.0,
  "status": "CONFIRMED"
}

###

### 5.6 Book a desk for two attendees - SCREENSHOT TEST 4
### A desk has capacity 1. Expected: 400 Bad Request.
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/bookings?memberId={{memberId}}&resourceId={{deskId}}
Content-Type: application/json
Accept: application/json

{
  "startDateTime": "{{testDate}}T11:00:00",
  "endDateTime": "{{testDate}}T12:00:00",
  "attendees": 2,
  "totalCost": 15.0,
  "status": "CONFIRMED"
}


### ==========================================================
### 6. UPDATE AND CANCEL BOOKINGS
### ==========================================================

### 6.1 Update a booking
### Replace the ID with a real booking ID. Use a valid, non-conflicting time.
PUT {{baseUrl}}/api/bookings/{{bookingId}}
Content-Type: application/json
Accept: application/json

{
  "startDateTime": "{{testDate}}T14:00:00",
  "endDateTime": "{{testDate}}T15:00:00",
  "attendees": 1,
  "status": "CONFIRMED"
}

###

### 6.2 Cancel a booking - SCREENSHOT TEST 6A
### Use the booking ID created in 5.3. Expected: 200 OK.
### Keep the same resource and time so that the slot can be rebooked.
PUT {{baseUrl}}/api/bookings/15
Content-Type: application/json
Accept: application/json

{
  "startDateTime": "{{testDate}}T09:00:00",
  "endDateTime": "{{testDate}}T10:00:00",
  "attendees": 1,
  "status": "CANCELLED"
}

###

### 6.3 Rebook the cancelled time slot - SCREENSHOT TEST 6B
### Expected: 201 Created if cancellation releases the slot.
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/bookings?memberId=1&resourceId=2
Content-Type: application/json
Accept: application/json

{
  "startDateTime": "{{testDate}}T09:00:00",
  "endDateTime": "{{testDate}}T10:00:00",
  "attendees": 1,
  "totalCost": 15.0,
  "status": "CONFIRMED"
}

### ==========================================================
### 7. UPDATE RESOURCE STATUS AND DELETE RESOURCE
### ==========================================================

### 7.1 Set the room OUT_OF_SERVICE
### This full update body assumes PUT requires all room fields.
PUT {{baseUrl}}/api/resources/{{roomId}}
Content-Type: application/json
Accept: application/json

{
  "name": "HTTP Test Meeting Room",
  "location": "Doha",
  "capacity": 8,
  "hourlyRate": 75.0,
  "status": "OUT_OF_SERVICE",
  "hasProjector": true,
  "hasVideoConference": true
}

###

### 7.2 Attempt to book the OUT_OF_SERVICE room - SCREENSHOT TEST 5
### Expected: 409 Conflict.
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/bookings?memberId={{memberId}}&resourceId={{roomId}}
Content-Type: application/json
Accept: application/json

{
  "startDateTime": "{{testDate}}T15:00:00",
  "endDateTime": "{{testDate}}T16:00:00",
  "attendees": 2,
  "totalCost": 75.0,
  "status": "CONFIRMED"
}

###

### 7.3 Attempt to delete a resource that has bookings
### Run after successfully creating the desk booking in 5.3.
### Expected: 409 Conflict.

DELETE {{baseUrl}}/api/resources/{{deskId}}
Accept: application/json


### ==========================================================
### 8. DUPLICATE MEMBER EMAIL TEST
### ==========================================================

### 8.1 Create the first member with this email
### Expected: 201 Created if this email does not already exist.
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/members
Content-Type: application/json
Accept: application/json

{
  "fullName": "Duplicate Test User",
  "email": "coworkhub.duplicate.20261121@example.com"
}

###

### 8.2 Create another member with the SAME email - SCREENSHOT TEST 8
### Expected: 409 Conflict.
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/members
Content-Type: application/json
Accept: application/json

{
  "fullName": "Duplicate Test User Two",
  "email": "coworkhub.duplicate.20261121@example.com"
}


### ==========================================================
### 9. OPTIONAL BOOKING DELETE - VERIFY BEFORE RUNNING
### ==========================================================
### The original project HTTP file included this optional request.
### Run ONLY if BookingController implements DELETE and permanent
### deletion is intended. Cancellation is preferred for booking history.

### 9.1 Delete booking by ID (optional)
DELETE {{baseUrl}}/api/bookings/{{bookingId}}
Accept: application/json


### ==========================================================
### 10. DOCKER DATA-PERSISTENCE CHECK (MANUAL)
### ==========================================================
### 1. Create a member or booking and note its ID.
### 2. In Terminal run: docker compose restart
### 3. Wait until backend starts again.
### 4. Run the GET request below.
### 5. Confirm that the member/booking data still exists.
### Do NOT run docker compose down -v; it deletes the named DB volume.

### 10.1 Get all members after Docker restart - SCREENSHOT TEST 9
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/members
Accept: application/json

###

### 10.2 Get all bookings after Docker restart
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/bookings
Accept: application/json


### ==========================================================
### 11. TESTING EVIDENCE SUMMARY FOR THE REPORT
### ==========================================================
### Test 1: 5.3 POST /api/bookings - valid booking - expected 201.
### Test 2: 5.4 POST /api/bookings - overlapping booking - expected 409.
### Test 3: 5.5 POST /api/bookings - invalid time - expected 400.
### Test 4: 5.6 POST /api/bookings - desk with 2 attendees - expected 400.
### Test 5: 7.2 POST /api/bookings - out-of-service resource - expected 409.
### Test 6: 6.2 PUT cancel (200), then 6.3 POST rebook (201).
### Test 7: 7.3 DELETE resource with bookings - expected 409.
### Test 8: 8.2 POST duplicate member email - expected 409.
### Test 9: 10.1 GET members after Docker restart - data persists.
### Take a screenshot of each response. Test 6 needs two response screenshots.
